`). That broke `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`, which expects `2.665` to round to `2.66`.\n- **Fix:** I created the branch `fix/money-round-half-even` and changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on commit `08d3cd5986` passed.\n- **PR:** I opened [PR #101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101) against main with code-owner as reviewer. A human approver signed off on the merge (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), as policy requires, and the PR merged at `08d3cd5986`.\n\nI couldn't look up FIN-212 because the advisory system doesn't recognise that ID, so the fix follows what the test and the docstring say.", "type": "text"}]}]}